  <h1>📋 My Planner — Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="sub">Effective date: September 5, 2026 · App: My Planner (https://accountnotfound-hub.github.io/planner-apper/)</div>

  <p>My Planner is a student planner app for organizing activities, tasks, and study time.
  This policy explains what information the app handles, why, and the choices you have.
  We keep it short and honest.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Account details:</b> a username you choose, and — if you sign up with a password —
        your email address. If you sign in with Google, we receive your Google account's
        name and email from Google Sign-In.</li>
    <li><b>Your planner content:</b> the activities, tasks, study sessions, notes, coins,
        and streaks you create in the app.</li>
    <li><b>Friends &amp; groups:</b> your share code, the friends you add, and messages you
        send in group chats you join.</li>
    <li><b>Google Calendar (optional):</b> only if you choose to connect it, the app asks
        Google for <b>read-only</b> access and imports your next two weeks of events into
        your planner. The app can never change or delete anything in your calendar. You can
        remove imported events at any time in Settings.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do NOT do</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul style="margin:0;">
      <li>We do <b>not</b> show ads.</li>
      <li>We do <b>not</b> sell your data to anyone.</li>
      <li>We do <b>not</b> track you across other apps or websites.</li>
      <li>Passwords are <b>never stored in readable form</b> — only a one-way hash.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
  <p>Planner data is stored on your own device and, for signed-in accounts, in
  Google Firebase (Firestore), which we use as our secure cloud database. Data in
  transit is protected with HTTPS. Group messages are visible to the members of that
  group. Access to account administration is restricted to the app's administrator.</p>

  <h2>Children and parents</h2>
  <p>My Planner is designed for students aged 13 and up. The app includes built-in
  parental controls (shop lock, photo proof for completed tasks, and email reports)
  which a parent or guardian can enable in Settings. If you are a parent and have any
  question about your child's data, contact us at the address below and we will help.</p>

  <h2>Deleting your account and data</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p style="margin:0 0 8px;"><b>In the app:</b> open <b>Settings → Delete my account</b>.
    This permanently removes your account and all of its planner data. It cannot be undone.</p>
    <p style="margin:0;"><b>By email:</b> if you can no longer access the app, email us at
    <a href="mailto:alisabri.19.2012@gmail.com">alisabri.19.2012@gmail.com</a> from the
    address linked to your account with the subject "Delete my account", and we will erase
    your data within 30 days.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this same address with an
  updated effective date, and important changes will be announced in the app's
  "What's new" section.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy or your data:
  <a href="mailto:alisabri.19.2012@gmail.com">alisabri.19.2012@gmail.com</a></p>
